WEBVTT

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.770
This must be a Vagan base...{This is a Vagan base...?}

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.860
No.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.030
This is Vagan itself.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.270
You are...

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.530
Welcome to Vagan.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:18.490
{OP}

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.930
todokasete kono mune ni

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.930
Let your voice reach my heart

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.440
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.440
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.860
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.860
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:35.610
samayoitsuzuketeita

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:35.610
I kept wandering

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.370
tachidomaru no mo mae ni susumu koto mo

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.370
Halting in your tracks and walking ahead proudly

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.840
atozusari na ki ga shiteta

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.840
both seemed too fearsome a choice

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.300
tojikomerareta shikakui sora no shita

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.300
Here on the board, where we are bound to

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.550
iki wo hisometeta

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.550
I tried to breathe softly to blend in

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:04.970
tsumetai hoho wo tsutawaru kako no yowasa nugutte

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:04.970
I swept away the weakness of the past trailing down my cheeks

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:11.440
hikari sasu basho he kono te wo nobasu yo

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:11.440
and held out my hands to the light

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.030
todokasete kono mune ni

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.030
Let your voice reach my heart

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.530
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.530
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.950
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.950
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.950
sagashitsuzuketeru

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.950
I kept searching

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.040
todokaseru sono mune ni

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.040
I will let my feelings and my voice

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.460
tashika na omoi boku no koe wo

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.460
reach your heart

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.880
owaranai genjitsu de

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.880
Through days without end

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.300
sakebitsuzuketeiku

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.300
I will be proud, be strong

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:47.140
ashita wo shinjite

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:47.140
and have faith in the future

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:55.510
Episode 37
 The World of Vagan

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.210
Are you at all curious?

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.550
So you can't converse with an enemy?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.800
No matter.{Very well, then.}

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.060
Behold.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:23.770
This is Second Moon, the Mars Sphere's largest colony.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:29.310
A symbol of Vagan, built by the strong feelings of those left behind.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.570
I created the ultimate army to take back Earth.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:38.230
Its technology, the morale of its soldiers, its organizational unity...

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.270
It's {top-ranked}peerless in every respect.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.240
Do you wonder why?

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:50.970
How did the people left behind on Mars obtain such military might?

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.690
Everything is ready.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.070
We'll take custody of the prisoner.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.330
No, there's no need for that.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.690
I'll take him myself.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:25.110
This person is special, you see.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:25.950
Yes, sir.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.290
How does it look?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.370
We're carrying out analysis.{We're now analyzing.}

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:40.150
We're looking into the possibility of creating a new Gundam from the data in the EXA-DB.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.810
A new Gundam?

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.690
You haven't heard?

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:49.710
Lord Ezelcant has ordered us to create a new Gundam with Vagan technology.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.490
It's even possible to create a Gundam from it?{It can even create a Gundam?}

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:59.180
The EXA-DB certainly is amazing.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:03.650
It's a legacy of forbidden technology from the old National Wars.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.830
So the wars themselves were folly,

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.910
but ironically, they pushed science and technology to their limits...

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:16.730
I presume that any single mobile suit from that era

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.820
would be far more powerful than any we have now.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.420
One pilot could control hundreds of units at once...

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.440
And they had even greater weapons of mass destruction.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.350
They had mastered every technology of war.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.100
So we've found just one fragment of a huge body of information?

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:35.900
Correct.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.060
And that's given Vagan its current level of technology.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:44.690
In that case... What if we were able to get it all?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.070
This war would probably...

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.030
Come to an end?{>a end}

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.950
I had no idea it was so powerful.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.650
The cursed treasure... EXA-DB!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.880
Guards, that's far enough. Leave us.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.690
Yes, sir.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.310
So that's him?

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.610
The boy you captured in the Earth Sphere.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.150
Th-This boy...

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.320
So you noticed?

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.570
Glaring at me won't change a thing.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:37.500
If I gave the word, your life would be over in an instant.{If I ordered it, your life would end in seconds.}

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.960
Why did you bring me here?!{What did you intend by bringing me here?!}{perhaps just "Why did you bring me here?}

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.280
So, you finally speak.{You finally spoke, eh?}

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:48.050
I want you to see for yourself, as a representative of the Earth Sphere:

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.760
The world of Vagan.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.430
But you've only just arrived.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:58.100
I've prepared a room. You should rest.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.250
This way.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.310
I'm Mary, your attendant.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:04.690
Nice to meet you.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.230
My attendant...?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.450
Okay, we're here.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:20.530
This is your room.{This is it.}

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.710
Huh? You're...

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:37.140
Oh, that's why you get to use this room.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:38.930
What?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.810
Your face. You look just like him.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.100
My face?

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:49.970
This is...

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.230
That's Lord Ezelcant's son.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:54.560
He died a long time ago.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.550
That must be why you're getting special treatment.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:08:02.290
Oh, why else would a prisoner of war get a grand room like this?{Otherwise, would a prisoner of war get a room like this?}

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.710
Now, take those clothes off and get changed.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.310
Where are you taking me?

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:29.260
Do you know why we launched a war against the Earth Federation?

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:30.990
You want to steal Earth, right?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.830
Steal Earth?

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:35.830
We're not stealing it. We're taking it back.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:40.410
We swore to return to our homeland, no matter what it took.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.540
To restore our dignity as humans.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.690
But you've killed so many people.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.590
Whatever your reason is, that doesn't make it right.{There's no reason that coud possibly justify that.}{I like your correction card, but I don't think a kid would speak like that}

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.210
Can you understand it?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:57.260
The suffering of those who struggle to live on even after receiving a death sentence.{The suffering of people who receive a death sentence, and keep living anyway?}

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.830
The Mars Sphere was the new frontier we dreamed of.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.100
But it was naught but an illusion.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:12.990
The failed terraforming, and the Mars Rays produced by magnetic storms, spread deadly diseases...

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:19.240
The people of the Mars Sphere bore children and continued our history,

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.540
even as we struggled with the fear of death.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:27.310
We lived on, hoping to someday return to Earth.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.890
That's why we decided to fight.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.130
To take back our homeland of Earth.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.650
That's the reason we fight.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:40.470
Now do you understand?{Can you understand it?}

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.870
But... but still, the Vegan have...{But even so, the Vagan...}

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:57.830
Take this with you.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:09:59.900
What is it?

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.960
An ID card and a communications terminal.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:07.750
With these, you can use the facilities in town and buy what you need.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.710
You're getting off here.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.030
Don't worry.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:13.530
I'll come get you later.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.580
Kio, learn about Vagan here.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:21.260
About the true nature of the enemy you all hate.

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:25.870
And just so we're clear, you're {being watched}under surveillance.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.770
There's no chance of escape.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.170
Wait!

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:56.690
I told you not to do this anymore!

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:03.540
Ow...

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:04.250
Here you go.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.030
Thank you.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.260
You're not from around here, are you?

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.920
Ow...

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:21.970
You're such a wimp.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.390
This is just a scratch.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:26.850
That'll do it.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.310
Where am I?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.100
My house.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.140
Make yourself at home.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.560
That was close.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.570
Things aren't easy around here.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:39.980
Everybody's pretty desperate.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.820
Don't blame them for it.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.070
What's wrong?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:47.870
Back to bed, Lu.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:49.740
Who are you?

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.580
I'm Kio.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.910
Kio Asuno.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.040
Kio, huh?  I'm Lu.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.130
You hurt?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.840
Yeah, but it's not bad.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.840
I guess you're okay.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.260
Thanks for everything.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:04.260
And your name...?

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.260
I'm Deen.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.510
Nice to meet you.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.100
What is it?

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.310
You're pretty cool.{I think I like you!}

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.600
Hey, Kio.  Wanna have dinner with us?

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.350
Let's talk!

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.230
Lu!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.320
Come on, brother.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.190
I wanna hear about the outside.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:23.440
That's okay, right?

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.610
It's fine with me.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.220
Um, so where are you from?

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.140
Someplace pretty far away.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.060
Do you go to school?

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.390
Yeah.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:57.230
What kind of school?  What do they teach?

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.770
What sports are you good at?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.110
Um well...

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.360
That's so wonderful.  I wanna go too.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.860
Everybody talking, fighting...

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.860
It must be so much fun.

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:11.740
You don't go to school?

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.450
Well...

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:14.450
How could you—{Hey}!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.790
Brother...

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:23.670
You know, don't you? With this disease, you have to stay in bed.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.260
Disease?

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.930
Because of the Mars Rays!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.970
Lord Ezelcant, that boy is the Gundam's pilot!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.850
Shouldn't we interrogate him to gather information?

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:40.520
It's not time for that yet.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.650
But we have to hurry!

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:45.360
I'm telling you to leave it to me.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.190
Yes, sir.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.960
So, how is it over there?

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.170
There?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:08.130
I mean, how much do the Mars Rays affect your colony?

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.180
Well...

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:11.760
You don't wanna talk about it, huh?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.760
That's okay.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.810
She won't last much longer.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.100
Three months at best.

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.860
It's not fair...

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.730
She has to die, and she hasn't done anything wrong.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.360
The disease... is it that bad?

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:33.910
Isn't there anything you can do about it?{You can't do something?}

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.530
Anything I can do?{Something?}

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.950
Even when there's medicine, it never finds its way to us.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:42.000
And it doesn't even really cure it.{And it never fully cures it.}

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.080
You just last a little longer.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:45.840
That's so...

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:50.510
Those damn Earthers get to live in a nice, safe place.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:55.010
They make us suffer like this, while they get to...

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.640
It's not fair!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:04.560
But I truly believe that someday Lord Ezelcant will lead us back to Earth.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.690
I'd really like to go. To Earth...

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.740
I have to get going.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:15.870
I see.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:20.660
Thanks.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:26.920
I haven't seen my sister that happy in a long time.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:34.640
But I don't want you to get involved with us anymore.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.180
Making a friend...

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.180
would just make it harder for her.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.100
But...

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.020
Brother!

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.190
Why do I have to stay in bed?{Why can't I be out of bed anymore?}

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.990
Even I... I know I'm gonna die soon!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.110
Lu!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:57.620
But... but... I want to meet more people!

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.620
I want to go more places!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.580
Can't I do that?

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.750
You still don't understand?

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:08.000
Even if you go someplace fun, or get to know people, it all comes to an end soon!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.670
It'll be harder to say goodbye...

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.920
You'll just be more scared of dying.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.430
But I don't mind.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:20.560
It's okay. I want to really live, even if it's just for a little while.{I want to have a real life, even if it's just for a little.}

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.020
I want a real life...

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.270
I want to talk to Kio again.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:31.860
I wanna talk with him more.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:02.890
Have you learned what the Mars Sphere is like?

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:09.480
People cherish their loved ones, and seek warmth from their families.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:13.320
But here, even such pure feelings are crushed.{pure feelings like those are crushed.}

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:20.740
For fear of loss, the Vagan people have smothered the emotion called love.{DYRL?}

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.660
But Deen and his sister...

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.080
The children you met?

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:31.040
It's true, everyone has human feelings when they're young.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:35.090
But as they grow, they cease to love others.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:38.590
They cease to be attached to their family or lovers.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:42.510
They become afraid to love someone from their {Ze}hearts.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:48.600
Can you hear them?  The cries of those who've been robbed of human feelings?

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.270
To us, dying is not sadness.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:55.480
Sadness is being unable to live as a human being.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.280
I'll tell you...

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.950
of my true intentions.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.420
This is not simply a war.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:15.420
In all the previous attacks, I've given them a chance to survive.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:20.800
I've put a question to the Earthers, who don't even know what it means to live.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:24.810
Whether they have the will to live... whether their lives have value.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.600
I cannot accept this!

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:37.780
Lord Ezelcant has gotten too attached to that boy!

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:42.450
True.  Even if he's a child, he's still an enemy pilot.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.410
Keep an eye on him.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.990
If it comes to it,{If we have to}

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.250
we'll kill him ourselves.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:50.960
Yes, sir!

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:04.890
Darling, he just looks so much like Romy to me...

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.890
I know.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.270
It's a cruel twist of fate.{Perhaps it's a trick of fate.}

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.900
Well?

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:20.150
The doctors say I have six months left.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:21.360
I see.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.460
I must hold out, no matter what.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.040
I must open Eden's door with my own hands.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.090
Yes. That's why we've kept on living...

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.010
Ever since the day we lost Romy.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.310
You'll have to say goodbye soon!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.690
You'll just be more scared of dying!

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.480
But I don't mind.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:01.360
It's okay. I want to really live, even if it's just for a little while.{I want to have a real life, even if it's just for a little.}

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.280
I want a real life...

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.030
Do you understand, Kio?

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:07.490
To us, dying is not sadness.

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:10.540
Sadness is being unable to live as a human being.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.470
By capturing the Gundam,

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:27.300
we stopped the Federation Forces' plans for a military build-up.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:30.510
Project Eden will move to its final phase.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:32.680
<i>The time has come.</i>

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.430
Yes, sir.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.100
<i>I've staked everything on this.</i>

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:41.940
<i>Do you remember, Zeheart?  The day I told you of this plan?</i>

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.030
I've never forgotten it for a second.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:50.450
To restore humanity to what it should be.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.370
That noble goal is my reason for fighting.

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:54.830
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.040
<i>I'll be relying on you.</i>

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.330
<i>I'm counting on your strength.</i>

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:02.210
Yes, Lord Ezelcant.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:11.760
